	"23": {
		"inputs": {
			"value": "Picture 1 is the scene. Picture 2 is the replacement object.\n\nReplace the {} in Picture 1 with the object from Picture 2.\n\nThe identity of the new object comes entirely from Picture 2: its shape, silhouette, geometry, proportions, structure, materials, colors, textures, patterns and every design detail are copied from Picture 2 exactly as they are. The output shows Picture 2's own form, whatever type, shape or size that object has.\n\nFrom Picture 1 the new object inherits only its placement: the same position in the frame, the same orientation and viewing angle, the same scale relative to the room, the same contact points with the floor and surrounding surfaces, the same perspective, and the scene's lighting with matching cast shadows.\n\nEverything else in Picture 1 stays pixel-identical: background, walls, floor, ceiling, windows, camera position, framing, and every other object and piece of furniture remains exactly where and as it is.\n\nPhotorealistic and seamless, as if Picture 2's object had been physically placed in that spot and photographed with the same camera."
		},
		"class_type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline",
		"_meta": {
			"title": "Prompt template"
		}
